# REQ-009: Audit Trail

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Medium
**Risk:** High (EMIS Web audit trail compatibility unconfirmed — see blocker below)
**Depends On:** REQ-001 (Unified Inbound Document Inbox)

---

## User Story

As a practice manager or authorised user,
I need a complete, tamper-evident audit trail of all user activity on documents,
So that I can investigate incidents, demonstrate compliance, and identify inappropriate access or actions.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Every user action on a document is recorded in an audit trail (see minimum fields below).
- [ ] Audit trail entries are immutable — no user can edit or delete an audit entry.
- [ ] Audit trail is accessible to users with the appropriate RBAC role (e.g. practice manager).
- [ ] Audit trail is viewable per document (all activity on a specific document) and per user (all document activity by a specific user).
- [ ] Audit trail entries are filed into EMIS Web from EMIS-X. *(Current architecture — see constraint below)*
- [ ] Audit trail is available for all document actions: view, create, upload, edit metadata, annotate, export, download, delete, file, code, assign, move folder, patient visibility toggle.

---

## Minimum Audit Fields (Baseline — to be confirmed in V1e)

> These fields are the working baseline. Final field specification to be confirmed during V1e Clinical Safety / IG design phase.

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `action` | The action performed (e.g. "View", "Annotate", "Export", "Delete") |
| `user_ern` | ERN of the user who performed the action |
| `document_ern` | ERN of the document acted upon |
| `document_type` | Type of document (e.g. discharge summary, test result) |
| `patient_ern` | ERN of the patient the document relates to |
| `timestamp` | ISO 8601 datetime of the action |
| `ip_address` | IP address of the user's session |
| `outcome` | Success or failure of the action |

**Forbidden fields in audit log:**
- Raw NHS number (use `patient_ern`)
- Internal database integer primary keys
- Document content or annotation free-text

