## EMIS Web Audit Trail Constraint

> ⚠️ **V1d PxD note (2026-05-22): Where audit trail data is stored remains under discussion.** The architecture described below (filing into EMIS Web) is the current working assumption but has not been confirmed. V1b/V1c/V1e agents must resolve this before implementation begins. PxD has proceeded on the basis that the audit data is accessible and queryable from EMIS-X, regardless of the underlying store.

> ⚠️ **Architectural constraint — open question for V1b.**
>
> EMIS-X currently has no native audit trail capability. Audit trail entries are filed into EMIS Web from EMIS-X. Before committing to this architecture for Document Management, V1b must confirm:
> - Whether the EMIS Web audit trail supports all minimum document management audit fields listed above
> - Whether EMIS Web audit trail entries filed from EMIS-X are queryable/viewable within EMIS-X (or only accessible via EMIS Web)
> - Whether filing audit entries into EMIS Web introduces latency or availability risk (i.e. if EMIS Web is unavailable, are audit entries lost?)
> - Whether a native EMIS-X audit store is required as a fallback or primary mechanism
>
> **This is a blocker for V1b.** Audit trail integrity is a DCB0129 and UK GDPR requirement — it cannot be left unresolved.

