## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — immutable audit log created before returning patient data; applies to all document access
- **CLIN-009:** Clinical Safety Logging — safety-critical events logged using ERN identifiers; no plain NHS numbers in logs

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-025:** Inappropriate document access goes undetected — data breach not identified; regulatory and patient safety implications
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-026:** Audit trail incomplete due to EMIS Web filing failure — audit entries lost when EMIS Web unavailable
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low–Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-027:** Audit trail tampered with — entries modified or deleted to conceal activity
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-024:** Audit entries are immutable once written; no update or delete operations permitted on audit records
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-025:** Audit entry written before action is completed (write-before-return pattern per CLIN-002)
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-026:** EMIS Web audit filing failure handling to be defined in V1b — must not result in silent loss of audit entries
  - **Type:** TBC at V1b
  - **Effectiveness:** TBC

