## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(c) legal obligation (NHS records management); Article 9(2)(h) health data
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — audit records containing patient ERNs are special category adjacent; stored encrypted at rest
- **IG-005:** Data Subject Rights — patients may request access to audit records relating to their own documents (subject access request)
- **IG-008:** Consent Management — audit trail changes to patient visibility toggles (REQ-008) must be auditable
- **IG-009:** Data Breach Notification — audit trail is the primary mechanism for detecting and evidencing data breaches within 72hr ICO notification window
- **IG-010:** Retention Policy Enforcement — audit records subject to NHS retention schedules; minimum 8 years for adult records

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 6(1)(c):** Legal obligation — NHS records management requirements
- **Article 5(1)(f):** Integrity and confidentiality — audit records protected from tampering
- **Article 30:** Records of processing activities — audit trail supports Article 30 obligations

