## PxD (Added by V1d)

> **Scope: Backend-only (Phase 1).** No audit trail viewer UI is in scope for Document Manager Core. The audit trail is a backend write capability — all document actions emit structured audit events (see Minimum Audit Fields). A viewer UI is intentionally deferred.
>
> **Future phase — Cross-EMIS-X Audit Section:** A common audit viewer should be built as a shared EMIS-X capability (not per-product). All EMIS-X products (including Document Manager) would feed into this central section. Document Manager emits audit events in the format required by that future shared viewer; no Document Manager–specific viewer will be built.
>
> **Impact on V3 coding:** No UI components to implement for REQ-009. The audit write pipeline (service + API) is the full Phase 1 delivery.

---

### User Flow

**Phase 1 (in scope):** No user-visible audit trail flow. Audit events are written automatically by backend services on every document action. No user interaction required or available.

**Future phase (out of scope for Phase 1):** A shared EMIS-X audit section will surface a filterable, exportable view of all audit events across products, accessible to authorised roles from a central location in EMIS-X navigation.

---

### Component Specifications

No UI components required for Phase 1.

**Future phase reference — design constraints to carry forward:**
- Audit events are read-only; no editing or deletion
- Forbidden fields must never be rendered: no NHS number, no ERN, no full IP address
- Timestamps in British format (DD MMM YYYY HH:mm) with `<time datetime="{ISO}">` for semantic markup
- Admin-only export (CSV); role-gated server-side
- Filter by event type and date range
- `jest-axe ^9.0.0` required when the shared viewer is built

